      "title": "Permission Engine: Investigating Missing Audit Logs and Privilege Escalation Due to Certificate Expiry",
      "content_summary": "This article addresses scenarios in Permission Engine where elevated privileges are observed alongside missing audit log entries, often linked to expired certificates or operator errors.",
      "content_body": "When an operator reports unexpected access denials or elevated privileges without corresponding audit trails, first verify the status of the SSL/TLS certificates used for secure logging transmission. Expired certificates can silently drop log events and break privilege inheritance checks. Check the certificate expiration dates in the Permission Engine configuration console. If certificates are expired, initiate a renewal immediately. Once renewed, perform a manual access review to confirm that privilege assignments align with current policy, and educate the operator on monitoring certificate health to prevent recurrence."
